<%- include('partials/head') %>

<section class="page-head">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <p class="smallcaps section-no">Paper &amp; Board · The Primary Desk</p>
    <h1>Every grade. Every scale.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Prime and secondary paper and board, traded across the UK, Europe and North America. We sell to mills, printers and converters; we buy redundant, surplus and recovered material outright.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <p class="section-no smallcaps">I. — Grades Handled</p>
    <div class="grade-table" role="table">
      <div class="grade-row" role="row"><div class="grade-cell head" role="cell">Prime reels &amp; sheets</div><div class="grade-cell" role="cell">Testliner, kraftliner, fluting; coated and uncoated woodfree; folding boxboard and other boards. Full production runs and regular programmes.</div></div>
      <div class="grade-row" role="row"><div class="grade-cell head" role="cell">Stocklots &amp; side-runs</div><div class="grade-cell" role="cell">Over-makings, trial runs, non-standard widths and grammages, single-lot clearances. Described honestly, sold without pretence.</div></div>
      <div class="grade-row" role="row"><div class="grade-cell head" role="cell">Redundant &amp; surplus</div><div class="grade-cell" role="cell">Aged stock, cancelled orders, customer rejections, warehouse clearances — purchased outright, in any volume.</div></div>
      <div class="grade-row" role="row"><div class="grade-cell head" role="cell">Recovered grades</div><div class="grade-cell" role="cell">Printed and unprinted waste, converter offcuts, baled grades for mill consumption. Regular collection programmes arranged.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-tinted">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <p class="section-no smallcaps">II. — Selling &amp; Buying</p>
    <div class="two-col">
      <div>
        <h2>We sell</h2>
        <p>Mills and converters buy from us because the material arrives as described. Specifications are stated plainly, loading is photographed where useful, and shipping documents are handled by people who read them.</p>
        <p><a class="quiet-link" href="/live-desk">Lots currently available</a></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>We buy</h2>
        <p>Holding redundant stock costs money every week. We make fair open-market offers, settle promptly, and collect anywhere in the UK and Europe with our own arranged haulage. One pallet or a full warehouse; the courtesy is the same.</p>
        <p><a class="quiet-link" href="/contact">Offer material to the desk</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="section-inner narrow">
    <p class="section-no smallcaps">III. — Collection of Redundant Stock</p>
    <p>Send a line describing the material — grade, approximate tonnage, location, a photograph if convenient. The desk replies with an indication quickly, usually the same day. If the numbers work, we arrange collection at our cost and settle on agreed weights.</p>
    <p><a class="btn" href="/contact">Describe your stock</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

